  "analysis": "The previous solution used an O(n^2) DP with E(j,i) = (E(j,i-1) + 1) / p_i, which is too slow for n up to 1e5 and can also risk overflow for extreme inputs. We need an O(n) or O(n log n) approach that scales to the largest datasets. A better formulation reveals a convex hull trick (CHT) opportunity.\n\nLet A_i = 1 / p_i and Pre[i] = product_{k=1..i} A_k. Define invPre[i] = 1 / Pre[i] and Q[t] = sum_{k=0..t} invPre[k] with Q(-1) = 0. For each i, the DP can be rewritten as:\n    dp[i] = Pre[i] * Q[i-1] + min_j ( dp[j] - Pre[i] * Q[j-1] ) + (i < n ? 1 : 0).\n\nThe term min_j ( dp[j] - Pre[i] * Q[j-1] ) is a minimum over lines of the form y = m_j * x + b_j where x = Pre[i], m_j = -Q[j-1], b_j = dp[j]. Since Q[j-1] is non-decreasing in j, the slopes m_j are non-increasing; furthermore, Pre[i] is non-decreasing in i. This is a perfect scenario for a monotone convex hull trick (CHT) with a pointer, giving an overall O(n) per dataset solution (plus the O(n) precomputations to build Pre and Q).\n\nWe will implement a robust CHT with long double precision to stay accurate and use it to compute dp efficiently without overflow in typical datasets (though extreme inputs could still be risky due to extremely large Pre[i], we rely on the problem data to keep values within a manageable range).\n",
  "plan": "Plan to implement an optimized O(n) per dataset solution using a monotone convex hull trick (CHT):\n1) Read each dataset (n and p[1..n]) until a line with 0.\n2) Compute A[i] = 1/p[i], Pre[i] = product of A[1..i], and invPre[i] = 1/Pre[i] with Pre[0] = 1.\n3) Compute Q[t] = sum_{k=0..t} invPre[k], for t = 0..n (so a_i = Q[i-1] for i>=1).\n4) Maintain a convex hull of lines with slopes m_j = -Q[j-1] and intercept b_j = dp[j], starting with j=0 (m_0 = 0, b_0 = 0).\n5) For i from 1 to n:\n   - min_y = hull.query(Pre[i])\n   - dp[i] = Pre[i] * Q[i-1] + min_y + (i < n ? 1 : 0)\n   - add a new line for j = i with m = -Q[i-1], b = dp[i]\n6) Output dp[n] with 10 decimal places.\n7) Provide complete C++17 code implementing the above and test against samples.\n",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp <<'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Line {\n    long double m, b; // y = m*x + b\n    long double eval(long double x) const { return m * x + b; }\n};\n\nstruct Hull {\n    vector<Line> lines;\n    size_t ptr = 0;\n    // Check whether l2 is unnecessary between l1 and l3\n    static bool isBad(const Line& l1, const Line& l2, const Line& l3) {\n        // Intersection x of l1 and l2: (b2 - b1) / (m1 - m2)\n        // Intersection x of l2 and l3: (b3 - b2) / (m2 - m3)\n        long double x12 = (l2.b - l1.b) / (l1.m - l2.m);\n        long double x23 = (l3.b - l2.b) / (l2.m - l3.m);\n        return x12 >= x23;\n    }\n\n    void addLine(long double m, long double b) {\n        Line nl{m, b};\n        // Slopes must be non-increasing for this to work\n        while (lines.size() >= 2 && isBad(lines[lines.size()-2], lines[lines.size()-1], nl)) {\n            lines.pop_back();\n            if (ptr > lines.size()-1) ptr = lines.size()-1;\n        }\n        lines.push_back(nl);\n    }\n\n    long double query(long double x) {\n        if (lines.empty()) return numeric_limits<long double>::infinity();\n        if (ptr >= lines.size()) ptr = lines.size()-1;\n        while (ptr + 1 < lines.size() && lines[ptr+1].eval(x) <= lines[ptr].eval(x)) ++ptr;\n        return lines[ptr].eval(x);\n    }\n};\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cout.setf(std::ios::fixed);\n    cout << setprecision(10);\n\n    int n;\n    while (cin >> n) {\n        if (n == 0) break;\n        vector<long double> p(n+1);\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            long double x; cin >> x; p[i] = x;\n        }\n        vector<long double> A(n+1);\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) A[i] = 1.0L / p[i];\n        vector<long double> Pre(n+1);\n        Pre[0] = 1.0L;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) Pre[i] = Pre[i-1] * A[i];\n        // invPre[i] = 1 / Pre[i], with invPre[0] = 1\n        vector<long double> invPre(n+1);\n        invPre[0] = 1.0L;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) invPre[i] = 1.0L / Pre[i];\n        // Q[t] = sum_{k=0..t} invPre[k], t in [0..n]\n        vector<long double> Q(n+1);\n        Q[0] = invPre[0];\n        for (int t = 1; t <= n; ++t) Q[t] = Q[t-1] + invPre[t];\n\n        vector<long double> dp(n+1, 0.0L);\n        Hull hull;\n        hull.addLine(0.0L, 0.0L); // j = 0: a_0 = Q[-1] = 0, so m = -a_0 = 0, b = dp[0] = 0\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            long double min_y = hull.query(Pre[i]);\n            long double ai = Q[i-1]; // a_i = Q(i-1)\n            dp[i] = Pre[i] * ai + min_y + ((i < n) ? 1.0L : 0.0L);\n            hull.addLine(-ai, dp[i]);\n        }\n        cout << (double)dp[n] << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n\ng++ -std=c++17 -O2 -pipe -static -s -o main main.cpp\n./main << EOF\n2\n0.50 0.40\n2\n0.70 0.60\n4\n0.99 1.00 1.00 0.01\n0\nEOF"
